NAME
       task_info, task_kill - inspect and stop tasks

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       int cervus_task_info(int pid, cervus_task_info_t *out);
       int cervus_task_kill(int pid);

DESCRIPTION
       task_info fills in the pid, parent, owner, capabilities, name,
       state, priority, accumulated runtime, resident size and creation
       time of one task. Walking the pid space is how ps, top and
       sysmon build their tables.

       task_kill stops a task outright, without the signal machinery.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, negative on failure.

ERRORS
       ESRCH   no such task
       EPERM   not permitted to inspect or stop that task

SEE ALSO
       ps(1), top(1), kill(2), procfs under /proc
